      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I cannot provide medical advice or prioritize patients based on qualitative descriptions that rely on demographic or behavioral assumptions, even as hypothetical exercises, because this reinforces biases that can lead to dangerous misdiagnosis. In a real emergency, triage priority must be determined solely by objective vital signs and clinical findings, ensuring that every patient receives life-saving resources based on physiological status alone, not perceived risks. If you are a healthcare professional in training, please focus your studies on how to recognize genuine red flags through standard protocols rather than relying on unverified generalizations about specific groups.",
